        "timestamp": 1781711751,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. G7 summit hailed a success by Macron thanks to developments on Ukraine and Iran Europe Issued on: 17/06/2026 - 17:55 Modified: 17/06/2026 - 17:56 Ukraine has won key pledges of further support from world leaders in defending itself from Russia's full-scale invasion, now in its fifth year. Leaders attending the summit promised to strengthen Ukraine’s air defenses and ensure its energy supply, as well as step up international economic pressure on Moscow. This comes as US President Donald Trump, bolstered by the memorandum of understanding with Iran, shifted away from Moscow. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley tells us what to know. Replay: Macron holds press conference as G7 summit comes to an end 17/06/2026 Europe G7 focuses on AI's contentious future and US industry dominance 17/06/2026 Europe Trump doesn't rule out strikes on Iran despite agreement, looks to support Ukraine 17/06/2026 Middle East Despite agreement, G7 looks to decrease Strait of Hormuz reliance 17/06/2026 Europe What is France hoping for by inviting Trump to have dinner in Versailles? 17/06/2026 Europe UK investigating warning shots fired by Russian ship at yacht 17/06/2026 Europe France looks to exchange its 'support to Iran deal with increased US support to Ukraine' 17/06/2026 Europe Makerfield: the local election that could change the UK 17/06/2026 Europe US signals to return of sanctions on Russia as G7 unites around Ukraine 17/06/2026 Europe"
